Bug: POP returns to a session with stale positions

Browsing sessions hold copies of references, not indexes into the live table.
After a reparse only the session that consumes the per-file
needsBrowsingStackRefresh flag is refreshed, so POP returns to a session with
stale positions. Needs index-based sessions (roadmap). Details in the Makefile.

What it looks like today, two hunks and nothing else: after the preloaded
buffer shifts the call site down a line, session 2 navigates to line 7
correctly, then POP to session 1 answers line 6 and a NEXT on that session
repeats line 6. Expected is 7 in both places.

Until 2026-09-23 the test did not get that far. Its commands.input started a
second c-xref with -fastupdate and no mode, which became an error in
6c0582e0, so the run died with "No mode given" before its first assertion.
Every request now goes to the one server process, and the -xref -create prime
is gone - verified from clean, the server parses on demand and the failure is
unchanged.
